# aibo — local developer credentials (template)
#
# Copy to `.env.dev` and fill in the keys you actually have:
#
#     cp .env.dev.example .env.dev
#
# `.env.dev` is gitignored. This file is the committed template and must never
# contain a real key.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How aibo reads these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# There is no dotenv loader in the binary, and deliberately so: §12 keeps
# credential handling in one place, and a second silent source of secrets is the
# kind of thing that later turns out to have been logged. These are ordinary
# environment variables, so `source` them into the shell that launches aibo:
#
#     set -a && . ./.env.dev && set +a && cargo run --bin aibo
#
# `EnvCredentials` (aibo-session) reads `AIBO_<PROVIDER>_API_KEY`, where
# `<PROVIDER>` is the provider **id**, uppercased, with `-` replaced by `_`.
#
# Note the id is not always the `backend = "…"` spelling in config.toml:
# `open-ai` is addressed as `openai`, `open-router` as `openrouter`, and
# `samba-nova` as `sambanova`. The variable names below use the ids.
#
# The env var is a *fallback*, consulted only when the credential store has no
# entry for that provider. A key saved in the settings window wins — so if a
# provider misbehaves, check whether a stored key is shadowing what is here.
#
# A provider also needs a `[[providers]]` entry in config.toml before aibo will
# build it; the key alone is not enough. Adding one in Settings does both.

# --- OpenAI (also the STT endpoint for gpt-transcribe) ---------------------
AIBO_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- OpenRouter: one key, many upstream vendors ---------------------------
AIBO_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Google Gemini, direct Generative Language API ------------------------
AIBO_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Anthropic ------------------------------------------------------------
AIBO_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- The fast providers ---------------------------------------------------
AIBO_GROQ_API_KEY=
AIBO_CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
AIBO_SAMBANOVA_API_KEY=
AIBO_XAI_API_KEY=

# --- Azure OpenAI ---------------------------------------------------------
# Also needs `deployment` and `api_version` in its `[[providers]]` entry (§10).
AIBO_AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not here on purpose
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# * **Codex / the ChatGPT subscription.** §3a authenticates by device code, not
#   by an API key, and stores a refreshable token pair. There is no variable to
#   set; use Sign in in the settings window.
# * **Bedrock and Vertex.** SigV4 and service-account JWTs are not bearer keys.
# * **Ollama and llama.cpp.** Local endpoints take no credential at all.
